{"type":"message","id":"3c175295","parentId":"53eb1e62","timestamp":"2026-04-05T00:01:31.546Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So `workspace-wxlee/` is an untracked directory that contains its own `.git` folder. This makes it a nested git repository (a git d conflict), not a submodule. This is causing `git add -A` to fail because git doesn't add nested git repositories by default.\n\nI need to remove this untracked git repository from the backup process. Options:\n1. Remove the `workspace-wxlee/` directory entirely from the parent git repo (add it to .gitignore)\n2. Recover it properly as a submodule if it should be tracked\n3. Exclude it from the backup\n\nLooking at the context, `workspace-wxlee/` seems like it might be a separate workspace directory that was created but shouldn't be part of the main `~/.openclaw` repository. It's causing issues with the backup.\n\nLet me check the .gitmodules file to see if it's supposed to be a submodule:","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_0ff2d9d7728d449fb6e8fb9d","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd ~/.openclaw && cat .gitmodules 2>/dev/null || echo \"No .gitmodules file\"","timeout":5}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"openrouter/free","usage":{"input":3954,"output":473,"cacheRead":12160,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":16587,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775347285336,"responseId":"gen-1775347286-6mfvlZ2JgJ0YCFSuUrNr"}}
